# A client buffers 63 fragments of message 2 (64512 bytes) while message 0 is
# missing. A datagram then carries all 1024 bytes of message 0, which fills
# the 65536-byte buffer exactly and is kept, and a 1-byte message 1, which
# would pass it and is ignored (reassembly rule 4). Message 0 is delivered;
# message 1 is delivered when it comes again.
endpoint client 0123456789abcdef 4800 1024 262144 200000 plain 0 0 0 0
